 * present. It does not take into account the bytes for storing length. Refer
 * to MQTT v3.1.1 algorithm for the implementation suggestion.
 *
 * A Remaining Length is encoded on at most MAX_LEN_BYTES bytes and can only
 * be decoded from bytes that were actually received by the caller, so the
 * walk below stops as soon as either limit is reached instead of running
 * through stale buffer content.
 *
 * Returns (usize) -1 when the length field is not terminated within those
 * limits, in which case the caller must reject the packet.
